  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN TRANSITIONS PROJECT - SUSTAINING PEACE AND DEVELOPMENT BEYOND MISSION WITHDRAWAL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UN Transitions Project (DCO, DPO, DPPA, UNDP) is a cross-pillar mechanism supporting UN transition processes involving a drawdown or withdrawal of a UN Mission. Its goal is to ensure that UN transitions result in host nations being better equipped to consolidate peacebuilding gains. It does so by supporting the UN System and partners to plan and manage UN transitions in a more pro-active, integrated and forward-looking way</narrative>
  </description>
